{"id":"18c1dc83c92f8d0bd04fa1786f4644d8b22ca210fcf3236d","commits":["8e1c8ddf64cf88adf078e39e33f542683101b43a","769bc647fab1b4c4e8a34acf8cb462fcbcc08bca","472fb41d7f8f8cc316022532b2c719eb4cacf7e7"],"user_facing":true,"description":"**`Principal` renamed to `AuthContext`.** The ephemeral per-request auth type is now `AuthContext`; `consumer_id` is widened to `UUID | None`. Update imports and type references.","type":"breaking","packages":["auth","protocols"]}
{"id":"18c1dc83d4596672419a3526ddfc4518ad955428b70a5a51","commits":["d8de2a1c9ba567e07685fb316aafb1513c0756f2","86ecb8fb78e1a2145eb8d8298cdd6e03da833ab9","a3947a4ae97baef1c6a7aa800d8026aa4e447572","18afd5ccdee18a22249ca9a66b19da4354c5559b","2d2163bb53ffbf4acb7794a46c996bdff6183950","f4e3804bec0da553b3d5bde909a1971983f6f9b5","5138eccf15df3b010f4f80fd3759d6560a2b9cd5","9e5e4f706f68a79c1eca238a831f5f591937cf3a","d8644f1c17d262403f87175f7b7efa0978298e7a","86b0b5ce903fd6853c303c3684eaa77b292e1d47","ebf2d2403d3b056572b903eded2f1d0763e780c7","84952b055fdc8e3667a9e416371cc106b58803ab","4d9c9e29981e1e2d41c407d18e1632b9dff26646","bf4fc62be0b501ac5e4b8838cced07c7831e4403"],"user_facing":true,"description":"**MCP and A2A endpoints now require authentication.** Every capability dispatch requires an authenticated context carrying the capability declared scope, drawn from a new scope vocabulary covering all namespaces. An API served without an authenticator exposes public surfaces only (such as agent-card discovery).","type":"breaking","packages":["a2a","api","auth","cli","incoming","mcp","protocols","services"]}
{"id":"18c1dc83e40cf0c4fecb6e9967af451fae633e277b3fa2fc","commits":["424652ab4046557a2f166b7ff3482ceaf1e6c188"],"user_facing":true,"description":"**`events.source` replaced by `events.principal_id`.** Every event names its acting principal via a NOT NULL foreign key; the NOTIFY payload and event query filters use `principal_id` instead of the free-text `source`. The idempotent-write dedup path on PostgreSQL now returns the existing persisted event id instead of a non-existent one.","type":"breaking","packages":[".","api","cli","dispatch","incoming","overseer","scheduler","services","trace"]}
{"id":"18c1dc83ecbec62f70619ffa64cc4f85b403ae80c6771288","commits":["3c255f169be75d1ff176501384ac86d295cbaf1e","c5a9a442faa7df6c4f03bb7e87e35a12f74b625b"],"user_facing":true,"description":"**Subscriptions are owned by principals.** `subscriptions.owner_run_id` is removed; ownership is a `principal_id` FK that cascades on owner deletion. `SubscribeParams` drops `owner_run_id`, and `list_subscriptions` gains a principal filter.","type":"breaking","packages":[".","dispatch","protocols","services"]}
{"id":"18c1dc83f5a7c72f250e785af7a94b089d5efb8560005400","commits":["1271f10c0cb5a7ddc4a8206351fa019d6dfc0d47","aef74f6b3cef9d76158c8a608c7fb325a36bb20c","b754924ab8cd1f9d893522c520b124aa62cf89f6","7f43aa2b11dbcdda71926181937305555179d587"],"user_facing":true,"description":"**Attribution parameters added to write paths.** `write_event`, `create_run`, and the inbox writers changed signatures to carry principal attribution, and `create_run` now takes a caller-supplied `run_id`.","type":"breaking","packages":[".","overseer","scheduler","services","trace"]}
{"id":"18c1dc83fe0b24ba0d41be2423a24f86af655f21e36e554d","commits":["42ad99524020bed7f633503c926dc3bc8fd5154a"],"user_facing":true,"description":"**CORS wildcard-with-credentials is rejected.** The API compositor requires an explicit origin allowlist or no CORS; a `*` origin combined with credentials is refused.","type":"breaking","packages":[".","agui","api","incoming","worker"]}
{"id":"18c1dc960c2594069e438d05ce4944f5ba27c5da8ec88ac7","commits":["abf59a7b2c4220df3b41f64085bd4b8157c49c2c"],"user_facing":true,"description":"**Legacy MCP stdio transport removed.** The MCP server is served over HTTP with per-request identity; the stdio path is gone.","type":"breaking","packages":["mcp"]}
{"id":"18c1dc961799b55aef2a8e6549094fef89f4d861076dcd4c","commits":["8b249358017fc428d64624bfbd3377e7c0e9393b","d22c0ba9ea9e64e12bd09ea7b371cdf30acad12d","22e6c5317797fd13e4011613f7e470d62e403e67","4d1efad146c2fdd57896ea3ebbee7aea9195dea4","08a31ed8aa22f298cd6412fa67e4efc97f94d61c","cb950b72ffc359f10793061c2a1001e0981bfb39","065688be0f862ea2cfe9935cb4465f7fbcaba442","83bc06c109bbb5195fadc56afce9de24ea902cd8","c87828f07f72ac9c29c7a294ff796dde4821a452","7d5206b032908da77b8a2889e97c0052d8bc9ddf","a5b36c4182ef26ddda0b6ef22863b58f110c203a","a7db21dab942548fbbd7949bb098872e6b7c8cff","348b762672f32887671e7981f4a0b4f83b27ce21","485103fb7a294151d0ee9ae96c66160d9255de93","d08be4d21ee336d653bf87c9c2c9d4093283fc13","20fa4d8066e726c061e112b7d1580c4ed2c75839"],"user_facing":true,"description":"**Unified identity model.** A new `principals` table gives every actor -- runs, consumers, sources, the system, and app-registered kinds -- a durable identity minted at birth. Runs, sources, and consumers record their creator (`runs.created_by`, `sources.created_by`, `consumers.principal_id`, inbox `resolved_by`); principal CRUD is exposed as capabilities gated by `principals:read`/`principals:manage`; and deletion pins historical actors, raising `PrincipalInUseError` when references remain.","type":"feature","packages":[".","api","auth","cli","dispatch","identity","incoming","protocols","services","trace"]}
{"id":"18c1dc96219f260b6955304f2d9a4f4881f787d88fbe5ae1","commits":["8ba9b6d33a464d15ecd53a8f08fda2f385cd56d0"],"user_facing":true,"description":"**AG-UI per-run access control.** The AG-UI SSE stream is restricted to the run creator or an operator.","type":"feature","packages":["agui","api"]}
{"id":"18c1dc962b1efe23e43f9bc651e14b069e8077508681a29a","commits":["44e051f6f259d5bc4827b2bc2a15e1850ad8c9a5","22ab3e9c652c8f6ba5dd8884d93083568675013b","1d9464c70cf07778519890013e4b0e253adedb43"],"user_facing":true,"description":"**MCP tools expose real parameter schemas.** FastMCP-served tools previously advertised a broken kwargs-envelope schema; they now serve each capability actual parameter schema and validate input strictly.","type":"fix","packages":["mcp"]}
{"id":"18c1dc9634658f93f7617030ec5843b9bfa7fa22f47eac7c","commits":["5d7f307532d9f1b5ee5825b3ab7c4ddd500474b5"],"user_facing":true,"description":"**MCP tools with tuple returns no longer crash.** Tool results that return a tuple (such as `fire_event`) now serialize correctly instead of crashing after the side effect ran.","type":"fix","packages":["mcp"]}
{"id":"18c1dc963d165bf9055db7e88810467e842ae9f5b50460d1","commits":["6603ef2a88e0dbae2539409a22bec67597d01493"],"user_facing":true,"description":"**Inbox reads work against PostgreSQL.** Inbox item `options` and `tags` are decoded via a jsonb codec, fixing reads that failed against a real PostgreSQL backend.","type":"fix","packages":["trace"]}
{"id":"18c1dc964622269b006e726edb2447d5882317852a1ffff4","commits":["0aeef843228a66a203ec49e827ed486b309447e1","b17439732962e6e631c87668c7d8c37afd8e5674"],"user_facing":true,"description":"**Crash-recovery events are attributed to the system principal.** Recovery-generated events no longer violate the new NOT NULL event attribution.","type":"fix","packages":[".","trace"]}
{"id":"18c1dc964f177b2110857a0c63314dbd86c25963aad538f4","commits":["6673e9263517946f0169f90e639f0a61f6cba2fd"],"user_facing":true,"description":"**Mounted sub-app session managers initialize on startup.** The composited application lifespan now forwards through to mounted sub-apps (requires fastware >= 0.5.0), so their session managers start correctly.","type":"fix","packages":[".","api"]}
{"id":"18c1dc96595194f300bd557a477c459a820fe779659c1c24","commits":["0630006c61753984ec2e3fb6ce95aef30195bbb7"],"user_facing":true,"description":"**Streaming token usage is reported for Anthropic and OpenAI providers.** Streamed responses now surface input and output token usage instead of dropping it.","type":"fix","packages":["transport"]}
